Z||000000||malacite||11-07-2001||09:51 PM||||are the t-tops for the fiero and the firebird the same?<P>thanks<P>------------------<BR>Malacite<P>Grendel-88 Fiero RIP<BR>'94 Saturn SW2 DOHC||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||11-07-2001||10:08 PM||||Nope. Not even close. Dodge Daytonas and Ford Mustangs use similar P-seals, though.<BR>P-seals are the fuzzy seals petween the glass and the front and rear moldings. <P>The "made for Fiero" ones are occasionally available. Not sure about now.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||286SE'S||11-08-2001||03:14 PM||||Those datona t-tops are really close in size<BR>to the ones on a Fiero just about 2 inches bigger from front to back and 3/4 inch wider. <BR>Just enough to make them not fit. They were also produced by cars and concepts (C&C) so<BR>there are many similarities.<BR>I never knew what people mean when they talked about P-seals. Now I know.<BR>check here for new P-seals: <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com/ttop.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroparts.com/ttop.html</A> ||||reg||1
